        "text_kyUgaB": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "MANUAL WELDING:",
            "enable_h1_tag": false,
            "heading_size": "h3",
            "description": "<p>EZG's welders' expertise and years of experience can meet most of your welding needs. We employ certified welders with unparalleled expertise who regularly surpass clients' highest standards. Our team is AWS certified in these two arc/resistance welding processes: </p><ul><li><strong>Metal Inert Gas (MIG) Welding:</strong> This process uses an electric arc between a wire electrode and metal parts to combine and weld the materials together. A shielding gas is released from the welding gun to protect the molten metal from atmospheric contamination. MIG welding uses a continuous wire electrode fed through a welding gun. </li><li><strong>Tungsten Intert Gas (TIG) Welding:</strong> This process also uses an electric arc to melt and join the metal parts together with an inert gas to shield the weld pool from contamination by the air. TIG welding utilizes a non-consumable tungsten electrode and a separate filler rod. </li></ul>",
            "desktop_content_position": "center-md",
            "desktop_content_alignment": "ta-left-md top-md",
            "desktop_column": "2",
